# Puppet Server Complete Load
# EL9/SIMP 6.7 uses OpenVox, not Perforce Puppet. The package is
# 'openvox-server'; nothing in the EL9 repos Provides 'puppetserver',
# so asking for the old name aborts the install.
# (openvox-agent DOES Provide 'puppet-agent', so agent deps still resolve.)
lynx
git
openvox-server
simp
simp-adapter
# simp-vendored-r10k is REQUIRED, despite nothing declaring an RPM dependency
# on it: `simp config` deploys every Puppet module by shelling out to
# /usr/share/simp/bin/r10k (simp-cli, environment/puppet_dir_env.rb). Without
# it, `simp config` dies on that line and no module can be deployed.
# Built by build/el9-patches/vendored-r10k/build-el9.sh.
simp-vendored-r10k
xorriso
syslinux-tftpboot
yum-utils

# In case of broken repo, these should be installed.
hdparm
kbd
# libhugetlbfs  # REMOVED: not packaged for EL9
policycoreutils
rootfiles
selinux-policy-targeted
setserial
sysfsutils

# Storage tooling required by the kickstart's partitioning layout.
# These are NOT runtime dependencies of @core/@minimal-environment, so a
# dependency-closure-derived package list prunes them off the media -- anaconda
# then aborts with "missing packages: lvm2". diskdetect.sh builds an LVM layout
# (volgroup/logvol) on ext4 with an EFI partition and optional LUKS.
lvm2
device-mapper-persistent-data
grub2-tools-extra
nvme-cli

# Don't install these
-rhn-check
-rhn-setup
-rhnsd
-sendmail
-subscription-manager
# EL9 pulls these into @minimal-environment/@core and they Require
# subscription-manager, which SIMP excludes -- the transaction then cannot
# resolve and anaconda drops to manual software selection. They are Red Hat
# Insights / subscription telemetry and have no place on a STIG'd, airgapped
# host, so exclude them explicitly.
-insights-client
-rhc
-subscription-manager-cockpit
-subscription-manager-rhsm-certificates
-sysklogd
-yum-rhn-plugin
%end
